{
  "_comment": [
    "The trustd service definition, and the trust store's own keys.",
    "",
    "Identity is Service (the daemon's own virtual account). trustd needs no privilege to do its job: it reads a",
    "file the ca-certificates package ships, reads the registry, and writes",
    "/system/retc/ssl. The one privilege granted to trustd itself is",
    "SeAuditPrivilege, below, so that it can write trustd.root.added,",
    ".removed and .distrusted (trustd.evman) when the effective root set",
    "changes; without it the store still changes and the record of it is",
    "lost, with a warning in the log. The grant is a policy record for",
    "trustd's service SID (the S-1-5-80 SID derived from 'trustd', as in",
    "prepare-store), so it reaches trustd alone and not LocalService, which",
    "timed and resolvd also run as. Nothing it holds is secret -- the root",
    "set is public,",
    "which is also why its socket is open to everyone. Private keys are",
    "deliberately not trustd's: a key holder is a signing oracle under",
    "compromise and wants the opposite security posture, so machine identity",
    "belongs to a future key service, not here.",
    "",
    "ExecStartPre runs prepare-store as SYSTEM (HookIdentity) to create",
    "/system/retc/ssl and hand it to trustd's service SID. peinit provisions",
    "/run/<service> and nothing else, and /system/retc is SYSTEM-owned, so a",
    "least-privileged service has no way to make itself a directory there.",
    "The alternative -- running trustd as SYSTEM -- would throw away exactly",
    "the property that makes a public-data daemon safe. See PEI-329.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0): trustd sends READY=1 once it has composed the",
    "store and rendered it. Anything that speaks TLS should carry",
    "Requires = [\"trustd\"], because on a live image /system/retc is empty",
    "every boot and an unrendered store means no trust at all.",
    "",
    "RestartPolicy is Always (2). A machine whose trust store is stale is",
    "one that cannot learn a certificate was revoked.",
    "",
    "The Trust keys are created here, empty, so that trustd's watch has a",
    "target the moment it starts and an operator can find the knobs. The",
    "roots themselves are NOT here: they are package data, because reg apply",
    "is additive and Mozilla's removals would otherwise linger for ever.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the trustd package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System"
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services"
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\trustd",
      "values": [
        {
          "name": "ImagePath",
          "type": "sz",
          "data": "/usr/sbin/trustd"
        },
        {
          "name": "Triggers",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": [
            "boot"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Identity",
          "type": "sz",
          "data": "Service"
        },
        {
          "name": "ExecStartPre",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": [
            "/usr/libexec/trustd/prepare-store"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "HookIdentity",
          "type": "sz",
          "data": "SYSTEM"
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "type": "dword",
          "data": 0
        },
        {
          "name": "RuntimeDirectories",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": [
            "trustd"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "RestartPolicy",
          "type": "dword",
          "data": 2
        },
        {
          "name": "ErrorControl",
          "type": "dword",
          "data": 0
        },
        {
          "name": "DisplayName",
          "type": "sz",
          "data": "Trust store"
        },
        {
          "name": "Description",
          "type": "sz",
          "data": "Composes the machine's CA trust from the shipped roots and the registry, and serves it"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Trust",
      "values": [
        {
          "name": "GenerateLinuxTrustFiles",
          "type": "dword",
          "data": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Trust\\Certificates"
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Trust\\Certificates\\Add"
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Trust\\Certificates\\Distrust"
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Generic"
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn"
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn\\Policy"
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\Generic\\Authn\\Policy\\S-1-5-80-158018673-1219163202-1628709498-2735078191-2367099888",
      "values": [
        {
          "name": "Privileges",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": [
            "SeAuditPrivilege"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
